    "message": "fix(mcp): harden the stdio server — line-size cap, tree-kill, protocol-abuse matrix (#219)\n\n- Byte-bounded line reader replaces readline: a message over 1 MiB is\n  rejected with -32700 and the reader resyncs at the next newline, so a\n  pathological client can never force unbounded buffering.\n- Reject JSON-RPC batches with a single -32600; validate jsonrpc version\n  and id type per JSON-RPC 2.0.\n- Kill whole process trees on cancel/timeout/overflow/shutdown: children\n  spawn detached (own group on POSIX; taskkill /T on Windows), and the\n  executor tracks live children for disposeAll() on EOF and SIGINT/SIGTERM,\n  so a tool that spawned the indexing backend cannot leak it.\n- 14 new tests: protocol-abuse matrix (oversize, batch, malformed shapes,\n  unknown _meta, concurrent cancels, sequential queue, notification storm,\n  idempotent initialize, partial frame at EOF) + grandchild reaping and\n  disposeAll() orphan-prevention. Full suite 749 passed / 2 skipped.\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>",
